WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Each CO2 fixed costs 3 ATP and 2 NADPH.

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.740
The light reactions pay that bill.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.040
Now the sun sets. At night, the chloroplast makes NADPH by burning sugar.

4
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.140
So why doesn't the loop spend it to build sugar right back?

5
00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:28.503
Suppose it did. The loop would build sugar while another pathway burns that same

6
00:00:28.503 --> 00:00:31.423
sugar. That is a futile cycle.

7
00:00:32.663 --> 00:00:36.703
So light itself flips the loop's switches, through three signals in the stroma.

8
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:39.977
Signal one starts at the thylakoid.

9
00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:46.117
In the light, it pumps protons from the stroma into the lumen, the space inside it.

10
00:00:47.157 --> 00:00:49.497
Pump after pump, protons leave the stroma.

11
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.140
Watch the stroma as the protons go, one after another.

12
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.820
Does the stroma's pH fall, or does it rise?

13
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.260
It rises, from about seven to eight.

14
00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.200
Signal two, in the textbook account, is magnesium.

15
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:15.900
Magnesium ions flow from the lumen into the stroma to balance the charge.

16
00:01:16.983 --> 00:01:18.903
Both signals act on Rubisco.

17
00:01:20.223 --> 00:01:25.423
A separate CO2 first joins a lysine on the enzyme, forming a carbamate.

18
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:31.643
The carbamate then holds a magnesium ion, and that pair builds the working active

19
00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:32.643
site.

20
00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:37.867
High pH helps the lysine react, and more magnesium completes the pair.

21
00:01:39.287 --> 00:01:43.607
So one CO2 switches Rubisco on, and a different one gets fixed.

22
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:50.560
A Rubisco that is not switched on clamps onto RuBP so tightly it shuts itself down.

23
00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:56.360
An ATP-burning chaperone, Rubisco activase, pries the sugar loose.

24
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.630
Signal three is the most elegant.

25
00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.570
Photosystem one, driven by light, makes reduced ferredoxin.

26
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:09.930
Through a reductase, ferredoxin then makes reduced thioredoxin.

27
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:16.473
In four Calvin enzymes, thioredoxin breaks a sulfur-to-sulfur bridge between two

28
00:02:16.473 --> 00:02:20.833
cysteines. Freed, each enzyme can take its active shape.

29
00:02:22.113 --> 00:02:25.493
One of them spends the ATP that rebuilds RuBP.

30
00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:32.327
Here is the rule. Each switch is thrown by a change that light itself makes in the

31
00:02:32.327 --> 00:02:37.147
stroma. So the loop builds sugar only while the light reactions run.

32
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.240
At nightfall, the light reactions stop, and thioredoxin is re-oxidized.

33
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:49.120
The sulfur bridges reform, the enzymes switch off, and the cycle quietly stalls.

34
00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:53.373
So the plant has wired its sugar factory to the sun.

35
00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:58.053
It builds while daylight pays the bill, and it rests through the dark.
